1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,069
Patchwork is a WebMCP-powered neighbourhood action exchange, created by Leonardo Santos-Macias. It

2
00:00:06,069 --> 00:00:12,138
helps people and browser agents turn good intentions into realistic plans while

3
00:00:12,138 --> 00:00:14,667
keeping consequential decisions explicitly human-controlled.

4
00:00:15,667 --> 00:00:20,400
Finding a useful way to help still means searching listings, comparing time,

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:25,133
and translating intent into a practical next step. Patchwork provides one visible

6
00:00:25,133 --> 00:00:27,500
workspace backed by structured demonstration records.

7
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:33,355
Discover keeps the original experience. Four WebMCP tools let an external browser

8
00:00:33,355 --> 00:00:38,210
agent search projects, assemble a visible plan, draft a neighbourhood need, and

9
00:00:38,210 --> 00:00:41,042
prepare a pledge without embedding another chatbot.

10
00:00:42,042 --> 00:00:46,089
Plan together adds a separate session workspace. The person can pin projects,

11
00:00:46,089 --> 00:00:50,135
set a combined time budget, and ask the agent to revise around

12
00:00:50,135 --> 00:00:52,833
those constraints without changing the saved Discover plan.

13
00:00:53,833 --> 00:00:58,833
In the deployed branch, the Codex in-app browser natively discovered exactly two

14
00:00:58,833 --> 00:01:03,833
tools after the tab switch: get workspace and propose plan revision. AbortSignal

15
00:01:03,833 --> 00:01:07,583
cleanup prevents tools from an inactive workflow remaining advertised.

16
00:01:08,583 --> 00:01:13,302
The agent reads revision two, preserves the pinned pantry, and proposes replacing

17
00:01:13,302 --> 00:01:18,021
the orchard with the one-hour repair table. Patchwork shows the full before-and-after

18
00:01:18,021 --> 00:01:21,167
difference. Nothing changes until Accept revision is selected.

19
00:01:22,167 --> 00:01:26,979
Action history distinguishes WebMCP tool calls from interface actions and records the

20
00:01:26,979 --> 00:01:31,792
workspace revision. It is intentionally described as a bounded local history, not

21
00:01:31,792 --> 00:01:35,000
proof of identity or a tamper-proof audit log.

22
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
When the two-hour orchard is pinned inside a one-hour budget, the tool

23
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
reports a constraint conflict. It does not silently remove the person's choice

24
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,333
or claim that an impossible plan succeeded.

25
00:01:47,333 --> 00:01:52,887
The original safety boundary remains. Pledge support returns confirmation required and never

26
00:01:52,887 --> 00:01:58,440
contacts an organizer. Proposed community needs also require a separate visible approval

27
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:00,292
action before device-local publication.

28
00:02:01,292 --> 00:02:06,777
The project uses React, TypeScript, and Vinext on Cloudflare Pages. Sixty-four application

29
00:02:06,777 --> 00:02:12,261
checks cover both workflows. Native browser records remain separate from shim-based automation,

30
00:02:12,261 --> 00:02:16,375
and the branch deployment and live smoke test passed.

31
00:02:17,375 --> 00:02:22,087
Patchwork shows a future open web where agents reduce coordination work without

32
00:02:22,087 --> 00:02:26,799
taking away human agency. Open the live site, inspect the public source,

33
00:02:26,799 --> 00:02:30,333
and try both documented workflows. Small actions. Shared momentum.
